#
# Declarative structural assertions for the imagination slice — the slice-resident
# test-DSL twin of the MUST / MUST-NOT invariants formerly hand-written in
# tests/test_imagination.py. Authored as gmeow: ontology data so the same
# annotation discipline and the native Rust harness (crates/slicetest) drive
# the test, not ad-hoc Python. Each assertion runs as a SPARQL ASK over the module
# graph (gmeow:scopeModule); every `must` ASK anchors on a concrete term IRI (no
# vacuous, fully-variable pattern); negative universals (no reality bit, no
# subPropertyOf, no out-of-band logic: triple) are MUST-NOT ASKs that FIND the
# forbidden pattern across the relevant triple positions.
#
# NAMESPACE: the imagination module IS migrated — its value class is
# typed with the logic: stereotype vocabulary (logic:AbstractIndividualType,
# logic:QualityValue), NOT gufo:. These cells mirror the module's CURRENT logic:
# shape.
#
# BY-REFERENCE (cell saByReferenceNoLogicTriples): this is a DYNAMIC, open
# universal, not a hand-listed blacklist. The forbidden thing is ANY logic:
# IRI in any triple position EXCEPT (a) the fixed gUFO stereotype IRIs
# (logic:Kind … logic:Disposition) and (b) the canonical class-declaration /
# typing / header markers the owl:->logic: authoring flip mandates (logic:Class,
# logic:ObjectProperty, … logic:Restriction — the owl:/rdfs: spellings are now the
# generated projection). A FILTER(STRSTARTS(... logic:) && ?t NOT IN (<allowed>))
# quantifies over the WHOLE module graph, so a future logic:World / modal-logic
# leak is still caught (logic:World is kept OUT of the allowed set) even though no
# such triple exists today.
#
# ONE invariant is unreachable by this module-scoped ASK harness and lives as a
# native Rust conformance twin in crates/validate/tests/conformance_cases/conformance_imagination.rs:
# slice_depends_on_is_exactly_kernel — set-equality over manifest.ttl, which
# run_structural_cell never loads (store = module.ttl + examples/ only).
#
# The annotation-completeness test (test_every_declared_term_is_annotated) is
# subsumed by the global `make validate` gate (SHACL Gmeow*Shape for the class
# and properties + the Rust structural_lint guardian for the value-vocab origin*
# individuals). Verified 2026-06-22 in the awareness twin of this migration:
# deleting a value-vocab INDIVIDUAL's rdfs:label tripped the Rust guardian
# ("error individual … is missing rdfs:label") and deleting a CLASS's rdfs:label
# tripped the SHACL guardian ("error class … is missing rdfs:label"), both
# reddening `make validate`. That pytest function is therefore deleted rather
# than migrated.
#

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/imagination/tests/> .

# --- 1a. Spine verbs are ObjectProperties with agent domain (MUST) -----------
ex:saSpineObjectPropertiesAgentDomain a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:imagines a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:Agent .
    gmeow:supposes a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:Agent .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Both imagination spine verbs (gmeow:imagines, gmeow:supposes) MUST be owl:ObjectProperty with rdfs:domain gmeow:Agent — agent→content attitudes (Principle 4)." .

# --- 1b. Spine verbs are OPEN-range and non-functional (MUST-NOT) -------------
ex:saSpineOpenRangeNotFunctional a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    VALUES ?p { gmeow:imagines gmeow:supposes }
    { ?p rdfs:range ?r . }
    UNION
    { ?rec logic:characterizes ?p ; logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty . }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "OPEN-RANGE (Principle 13): neither gmeow:imagines nor gmeow:supposes MUST assert an rdfs:range, and neither MUST be functional — an agent imagines and supposes many things at once." .

# --- 2. Spine is FLAT and decoupled (MUST-NOT) -------------------------------
ex:saSpineFlatAndDecoupled a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    VALUES ?p { gmeow:imagines gmeow:supposes }
    ?p rdfs:subPropertyOf ?super .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "FLAT spine (Principle 4): neither gmeow:imagines nor gmeow:supposes MUST declare an rdfs:subPropertyOf — two distinct attitudes, not a hierarchy, and crucially NOT sub-properties of the doxastic spine (believes / accepts); imagining and supposing assert neither truth nor pragmatic commitment." .

# --- 3. ContentOrigin is a logic:AbstractIndividualType ⊑ QualityValue (MUST) -
ex:saContentOriginAbstractIndividualType a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:ContentOrigin a owl:Class , logic:AbstractIndividualType ;
        rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:ContentOrigin MUST be an owl:Class, a logic:AbstractIndividualType, and a subClassOf logic:QualityValue — the value-vocabulary genus shared with gmeow:MentalProcessType / gmeow:QuestionType (Principle 9, no overtyping); the stereotype namespace is logic: after the gufo→logic migration." .

# --- 4. The six content-origin individuals are seeded (MUST) -----------------
ex:saContentOriginIndividualsSeeded a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:originPerceived  a gmeow:ContentOrigin .
    gmeow:originRemembered a gmeow:ContentOrigin .
    gmeow:originBelieved   a gmeow:ContentOrigin .
    gmeow:originImagined   a gmeow:ContentOrigin .
    gmeow:originSupposed   a gmeow:ContentOrigin .
    gmeow:originGenerated  a gmeow:ContentOrigin .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The six content-origin values MUST be individuals of gmeow:ContentOrigin — a closed-but-open value vocabulary." .

# --- 5. Content-origin individuals are NOT subclasses/classes (MUST-NOT) ------
ex:saContentOriginIndividualsNotSubclasses a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    VALUES ?i {
        gmeow:originPerceived gmeow:originRemembered gmeow:originBelieved
        gmeow:originImagined gmeow:originSupposed gmeow:originGenerated
    }
    { ?i rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:ContentOrigin . }
    UNION
    { ?i a owl:Class . }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Value-vocab discipline (Principle 9, no overtyping): NO origin value is a subClassOf gmeow:ContentOrigin nor typed an owl:Class — each is an individual." .

# --- 6a. contentOrigin is an ObjectProperty ranging over ContentOrigin (MUST) -
ex:saContentOriginPropertyRange a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:contentOrigin a owl:ObjectProperty ;
        rdfs:range gmeow:ContentOrigin .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:contentOrigin MUST be an owl:ObjectProperty ranging over gmeow:ContentOrigin." .

# --- 6b. contentOrigin keeps an OPEN domain and is non-functional (MUST-NOT) --
ex:saContentOriginPropertyOpenDomain a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    { gmeow:contentOrigin rdfs:domain ?d . }
    UNION
    { ?rec logic:characterizes gmeow:contentOrigin ; logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty . }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "OPEN-DOMAIN (Principle 9 / Principle 13): gmeow:contentOrigin MUST assert NO rdfs:domain (content may be a claim, a proposition, or anything) and MUST NOT be functional (vantage-indexed)." .

# --- 7a. imaginedWorld is an ObjectProperty (MUST) ---------------------------
ex:saImaginedWorldObjectProperty a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK { gmeow:imaginedWorld a owl:ObjectProperty . }""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:imaginedWorld MUST be an owl:ObjectProperty." .

# --- 7b. imaginedWorld has BOTH ends open and is non-functional (MUST-NOT) ----
ex:saImaginedWorldOpenDomainAndRange a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    { gmeow:imaginedWorld rdfs:domain ?d . }
    UNION
    { gmeow:imaginedWorld rdfs:range ?r . }
    UNION
    { ?rec logic:characterizes gmeow:imaginedWorld ; logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty . }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "BOTH ends OPEN (Principle 5): gmeow:imaginedWorld MUST assert no rdfs:domain and no rdfs:range (the logic:World target is carried by reference) and MUST NOT be functional — one rehearsal may branch into several worlds." .

# --- 8. No reality or truth bit (MUST-NOT) -----------------------------------
ex:saNoRealityOrTruthBit a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    VALUES ?t {
        gmeow:isReal gmeow:isImaginary gmeow:isGenerated
        gmeow:isFake gmeow:isTrue gmeow:isFalse
    }
    { ?t ?p ?o . } UNION { ?s ?t ?o . } UNION { ?s ?p ?t . }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "No reality or truth bit (Principle 9): reality-monitoring is a gmeow:contentOrigin value, so none of isReal / isImaginary / isGenerated / isFake / isTrue / isFalse MUST appear in ANY triple position." .

# --- 9. No new content class is minted (MUST-NOT) ----------------------------
ex:saNoNewContentClass a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    VALUES ?c { gmeow:Supposition gmeow:ImaginedContent gmeow:ImaginativeContent }
    ?c a owl:Class .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The slice mints NO new content-mode class (the attitude verbs plus the originImagined / originSupposed markers carry the as-if): no gmeow:Supposition / gmeow:ImaginedContent / gmeow:ImaginativeContent MUST be declared an owl:Class." .

# --- 10. By-reference: no out-of-band logic: triple (MUST-NOT, DYNAMIC) -------
ex:saByReferenceNoLogicTriples a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    { ?t ?p ?o . } UNION { ?s ?t ?o . } UNION { ?s ?p ?t . }
    FILTER( isIRI(?t) && STRSTARTS(STR(?t), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/") )
    FILTER( ?t NOT IN (
        logic:Kind, logic:SubKind, logic:Phase, logic:Role, logic:Category,
        logic:Mixin, logic:RoleMixin, logic:PhaseMixin, logic:Event,
        logic:Situation, logic:AbstractIndividualType, logic:Relator,
        logic:QualityValue, logic:Mode, logic:Disposition,
        logic:Class, logic:ObjectProperty, logic:DatatypeProperty,
        logic:AnnotationProperty, logic:NamedIndividual, logic:Ontology,
        logic:Thing, logic:Nothing, logic:Restriction
    ) )
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "By-reference discipline (Principle 5): the module MUST assert NO triple whose subject, predicate, or object is a logic: IRI EXCEPT (a) the gUFO stereotype vocabulary (logic:Kind … logic:Disposition — identity/rigidity typing) and (b) the canonical class-declaration / typing / header markers the owl:→logic: authoring flip now mandates (logic:Class, logic:ObjectProperty, logic:DatatypeProperty, logic:AnnotationProperty, logic:NamedIndividual, logic:Ontology, logic:Thing, logic:Nothing, logic:Restriction — whose owl:/rdfs: spellings are the GENERATED projection, Principle 17). Both are the module's OWN declaration surface, not modal-world dependencies. This is a DYNAMIC universal (a FILTER over every logic: node in any position), NOT a hand-listed blacklist. logic:World is deliberately kept OUT of the allowed set: imagination consumes the counterfactual-world machinery strictly BY REFERENCE (documented in prose, never a triple), so a future logic:World / modal-logic leak triple is still caught — the invariant stays non-vacuous." .
